    {
      "id": "be0d9cd2-fd84-474d-ba42-4a8ed99d5ecd",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Java 8 Changes\n\n### New features\n\n1. Lambda expression & Functional Interfaces\n2. Named Lambda expression aka Method Reference\n3. Default Methods _(Supports backward compatibility)_\n4. for each enhancement\n5. Stream & Collector for data processing\n6. Type inference enhancement for lambda expresion\n7. Annotation type changes introducing `TYPE_USE`, `TYPE_PARAMETER` and Repeatable Annotation\n8. Spliterator\n9. Concurrency & MultiThreading\n    - DS\n        - Concurrent HashMap\n            - Concurrent HashMap changed from segment locks to fine-grained locks\n            - Introduced methods like reduce(), search()\n        - Map\n            - Introduced new methods map.compute*(), merge(), forEach()\n    - Framework\n        - ForkJoin\n            - Introduced ForkJoin.commonpool() for parallelStream() and CompleteableFuture.\n        - Executors\n            - Introduced work Stealing Pool\n        - Locks\n            - StampedLock\n10. CompleteableFuture\n11. Some New classes \n    - Optional\n    - Time APIs\n        - Core (Local)\n            - LocalDate\n            - LocalTime\n            - LocalDateTime\n        - Timezone / Offset\n            - ZonedDateTime\n            - OffsetDateTime\n            - OffsetTime\n        - Instant & Clock\n            - Instant\n            - Clock\n        - Duration / Period\n            - Duration\n            - Period\n        - Zone\n            - ZoneId\n            - ZoneOffset\n        - Year / Month Variants\n            - Year\n            - YearMonth\n            - MonthDay\n        - Enum\n            - Month\n            - DayOfWeek\n        - Formatting & Parsing\n            - DateTimeFormatter\n            - FormatStyle\n        - Temporal (Advanced / Framework-level)\n            - Temporal\n            - TemporalAccessor\n            - TemporalAdjuster\n            - TemporalAdjusters\n            - TemporalAmount\n            - TemporalField\n            - TemporalUnit\n        - Chronology (Alternate calendars)\n            - Chronology\n            - ChronoLocalDate\n            - ChronoLocalDateTime\n            - ChronoZonedDateTime\n            - IsoChronology\n        - Exception\n            - DateTimeException\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "be0d9cd2-fd84-474d-ba42-4a8ed99d5ecd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "894142c3-ce31-4a8b-8679-87068718b6fd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Anonymous class\r\n\r\n\r\n//Before Java 8, we used to create anonymous classes to implement functional interfaces (interfaces with a single abstract method).\r\ninterface Printer {\r\n    void print();\r\n}\r\n\r\nPrinter printer = new Printer() {\r\n    @Override\r\n    public void print() {\r\n        System.out.println(\"Hello, World! From Printer\");\r\n    }\r\n};\r\n\r\npublic void printSimple(Printer printer) {\r\n    printer.print();\r\n}\r\n\r\nprintSimple(printer);\r\n\r\n\r\n// Lambda expression => Replacement for only simple Anononymous classes\r\n\r\n// Simple Lambda expression\r\n\r\n@FunctionalInterface\r\ninterface Display {\r\n    void show();\r\n}\r\n\r\npublic void simpleDisplay(Display display) {\r\n    display.show();\r\n}\r\n\r\nDisplay display = () -> System.out.println(\"Hello, World! From Display\");\r\n\r\nsimpleDisplay(display);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "9573f9ff-d7c2-4d1e-bf2f-7b00fa719b5d",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "import java.util.function.*;\r\n\r\n// ===================== Core Functional Interfaces =====================\r\n\r\n// 1. Function<T, R> — takes T, returns R\r\nFunction<String, Integer> strLength = String::length;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Function: \" + strLength.apply(\"Hello\")); // 5\r\n\r\n// andThen / compose\r\nFunction<Integer, Integer> doubleIt = x -> x * 2;\r\nFunction<Integer, Integer> addTen = x -> x + 10;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"andThen: \" + doubleIt.andThen(addTen).apply(3));  // 16\r\nSystem.out.println(\"compose: \" + doubleIt.compose(addTen).apply(3));  // 26\r\n\r\n// 2. Consumer<T> — takes T, returns void\r\nConsumer<String> printer = s -> System.out.println(\"Consumer: \" + s);\r\nprinter.accept(\"Hello\");\r\n\r\nConsumer<String> shout = s -> System.out.println(\"!\" + s.toUpperCase() + \"!\");\r\nprinter.andThen(shout).accept(\"chain\"); // both run in sequence\r\n\r\n// 3. Supplier<T> — takes nothing, returns T\r\nSupplier<Double> randomSupplier = Math::random;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Supplier: \" + randomSupplier.get());\r\n\r\n// 4. Predicate<T> — takes T, returns boolean\r\nPredicate<String> isEmpty = String::isEmpty;\r\nPredicate<String> isShort = s -> s.length() < 5;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Predicate: \" + isEmpty.test(\"\"));          // true\r\nSystem.out.println(\"and: \" + isEmpty.negate().and(isShort).test(\"Hi\")); // true\r\nSystem.out.println(\"or: \" + isEmpty.or(isShort).test(\"\"));     // true\r\n\r\n// 5. BiFunction<T, U, R> — takes T and U, returns R\r\nBiFunction<String, String, String> concat = String::concat;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"BiFunction: \" + concat.apply(\"Hello, \", \"World\")); // Hello, World\r\n\r\n// 6. UnaryOperator<T> — Function<T, T>\r\nUnaryOperator<String> toUpper = String::toUpperCase;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"UnaryOperator: \" + toUpper.apply(\"java\")); // JAVA\r\n\r\n// 7. BinaryOperator<T> — BiFunction<T, T, T>\r\nBinaryOperator<Integer> max = BinaryOperator.maxBy(Comparator.naturalOrder());\r\nBinaryOperator<Integer> min = BinaryOperator.minBy(Comparator.naturalOrder());\r\nSystem.out.println(\"BinaryOperator max: \" + max.apply(3, 7)); // 7\r\nSystem.out.println(\"BinaryOperator min: \" + min.apply(3, 7)); // 3\r\n\r\n// 8. BiConsumer<T, U> — takes T and U, returns void\r\nBiConsumer<String, Integer> printEntry = (k, v) -> System.out.println(\"BiConsumer: \" + k + \"=\" + v);\r\nprintEntry.accept(\"age\", 25);\r\n\r\n// 9. BiPredicate<T, U> — takes T and U, returns boolean\r\nBiPredicate<String, Integer> lengthCheck = (s, len) -> s.length() == len;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"BiPredicate: \" + lengthCheck.test(\"Java\", 4)); // true\r\n\r\n// ===================== Primitive Specializations =====================\r\n\r\n// --- Int ---\r\nIntFunction<String> intToStr = i -> \"Number: \" + i;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntFunction: \" + intToStr.apply(42));\r\n\r\nIntConsumer intPrint = i -> System.out.println(\"IntConsumer: \" + i);\r\nintPrint.accept(10);\r\n\r\nIntSupplier intSupply = () -> 99;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntSupplier: \" + intSupply.getAsInt());\r\n\r\nIntPredicate isPositive = i -> i > 0;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntPredicate: \" + isPositive.test(5)); // true\r\n\r\nIntUnaryOperator square = i -> i * i;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntUnaryOperator: \" + square.applyAsInt(6)); // 36\r\n\r\nIntBinaryOperator intSum = Integer::sum;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntBinaryOperator: \" + intSum.applyAsInt(3, 4)); // 7\r\n\r\nToIntFunction<String> strToInt = String::length;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToIntFunction: \" + strToInt.applyAsInt(\"Hello\")); // 5\r\n\r\nToIntBiFunction<String, String> combinedLen = (a, b) -> a.length() + b.length();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToIntBiFunction: \" + combinedLen.applyAsInt(\"Hi\", \"There\")); // 7\r\n\r\nIntToLongFunction intToLong = i -> (long) i * 1_000_000;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntToLongFunction: \" + intToLong.applyAsLong(5)); // 5000000\r\n\r\nIntToDoubleFunction intToDouble = i -> i / 3.0;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"IntToDoubleFunction: \" + intToDouble.applyAsDouble(10)); // 3.333...\r\n\r\n// --- Long ---\r\nLongFunction<String> longToStr = l -> \"Long: \" + l;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongFunction: \" + longToStr.apply(100L));\r\n\r\nLongConsumer longPrint = l -> System.out.println(\"LongConsumer: \" + l);\r\nlongPrint.accept(999L);\r\n\r\nLongSupplier longSupply = System::currentTimeMillis;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongSupplier: \" + longSupply.getAsLong());\r\n\r\nLongPredicate isEvenLong = l -> l % 2 == 0;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongPredicate: \" + isEvenLong.test(42L)); // true\r\n\r\nLongUnaryOperator doubleLong = l -> l * 2;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongUnaryOperator: \" + doubleLong.applyAsLong(50L)); // 100\r\n\r\nLongBinaryOperator longMax = Math::max;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongBinaryOperator: \" + longMax.applyAsLong(10L, 20L)); // 20\r\n\r\nToLongFunction<String> hashLong = s -> (long) s.hashCode();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToLongFunction: \" + hashLong.applyAsLong(\"test\"));\r\n\r\nToLongBiFunction<String, String> combinedHash = (a, b) -> (long) a.hashCode() + b.hashCode();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToLongBiFunction: \" + combinedHash.applyAsLong(\"a\", \"b\"));\r\n\r\nLongToIntFunction longToInt = l -> (int) (l % Integer.MAX_VALUE);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongToIntFunction: \" + longToInt.applyAsInt(123456789L));\r\n\r\nLongToDoubleFunction longToDouble = l -> l * 1.5;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"LongToDoubleFunction: \" + longToDouble.applyAsDouble(10L)); // 15.0\r\n\r\n// --- Double ---\r\nDoubleFunction<String> dblToStr = d -> String.format(\"%.2f\", d);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleFunction: \" + dblToStr.apply(3.14159));\r\n\r\nDoubleConsumer dblPrint = d -> System.out.println(\"DoubleConsumer: \" + d);\r\ndblPrint.accept(2.718);\r\n\r\nDoubleSupplier dblSupply = Math::random;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleSupplier: \" + dblSupply.getAsDouble());\r\n\r\nDoublePredicate isWhole = d -> d == Math.floor(d);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoublePredicate: \" + isWhole.test(5.0)); // true\r\n\r\nDoubleUnaryOperator sqrt = Math::sqrt;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleUnaryOperator: \" + sqrt.applyAsDouble(16.0)); // 4.0\r\n\r\nDoubleBinaryOperator power = Math::pow;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleBinaryOperator: \" + power.applyAsDouble(2.0, 10.0)); // 1024.0\r\n\r\nToDoubleFunction<String> parseDouble = Double::parseDouble;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToDoubleFunction: \" + parseDouble.applyAsDouble(\"3.14\")); // 3.14\r\n\r\nToDoubleBiFunction<Integer, Integer> avg = (a, b) -> (a + b) / 2.0;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"ToDoubleBiFunction: \" + avg.applyAsDouble(3, 7)); // 5.0\r\n\r\nDoubleToIntFunction truncate = d -> (int) d;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleToIntFunction: \" + truncate.applyAsInt(9.99)); // 9\r\n\r\nDoubleToLongFunction roundLong = d -> Math.round(d);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"DoubleToLongFunction: \" + roundLong.applyAsLong(9.99)); // 10\r\n\r\n// --- Boolean ---\r\nBooleanSupplier boolSupply = () -> true;\r\nSystem.out.println(\"BooleanSupplier: \" + boolSupply.getAsBoolean());\r\n\r\n// --- Obj+Primitive Consumers ---\r\nObjIntConsumer<String> repeatPrint = (s, n) -> System.out.println(\"ObjIntConsumer: \" + s.repeat(n));\r\nrepeatPrint.accept(\"ab\", 3); // ababab\r\n\r\nObjLongConsumer<String> tagLong = (s, l) -> System.out.println(\"ObjLongConsumer: \" + s + \"=\" + l);\r\ntagLong.accept(\"timestamp\", System.currentTimeMillis());\r\n\r\nObjDoubleConsumer<String> tagDbl = (s, d) -> System.out.println(\"ObjDoubleConsumer: \" + s + \"=\" + d);\r\ntagDbl.accept(\"pi\", 3.14159);",
      "metadata": {
